\title{Even integers are countable}
\date{2026-03-12T14:04:12Z}
\tag{discrete}

\import{discrete-macros}

\taxon{Example}
\p{The set #{2\N} of all even natural numbers is countably infinite, since #{f(n) = 2n} is a bijection between #{\N} and #{2\N}: ##{\begin{array}{cccccc}
      \N: & 0 & 1 & 2 & 3 & \dots \\
         & \updownarrow& \updownarrow& \updownarrow& \updownarrow \\
      2\N: & 0 & 2 & 4 & 6 & \dots
    \end{array}}}


